To map B2C users and save all user-related information in an on-premises database, you can follow these steps:


---

1. Understand Azure B2C User Management

Azure Active Directory B2C (Azure AD B2C) is used to manage user identities. To save and map B2C users to an on-premises database, you need to:

Capture user data from Azure AD B2C.

Synchronize or save this data in your database.



---

2. Steps to Map and Save User Data

Step 1: Configure Azure B2C to Collect User Data

Custom Attributes: Define custom attributes in Azure B2C if you need extra fields beyond standard attributes (e.g., UserID, roles).

User Flows or Custom Policies: Use these to ensure user input is captured during registration/sign-in.


Step 2: Use Azure B2C Webhooks or APIs

Graph API:

Use the Microsoft Graph API to retrieve user data from Azure AD B2C.

Query user properties like ID, email, name, etc., and sync this data.


Example Graph API Call:

GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/users
Authorization: Bearer <AccessToken>

Learn more: Microsoft Graph API Users


Step 3: Create a Backend to Map and Save Data

Build an API or backend service to interact with both Azure B2C and your database.

1. Authenticate your app using client credentials or an app registration in Azure B2C.


2. Fetch user data using the Graph API or Azure B2C events.


3. Save the user data in your on-premises database.




Step 4: Save Data to On-Premises Database

Create a table to store user-related data:

CREATE TABLE B2CUsers (
    UserID NVARCHAR(50) PRIMARY KEY,
    Name NVARCHAR(100),
    Email NVARCHAR(100),
    PhoneNumber NVARCHAR(15),
    Role NVARCHAR(50),
    CreatedDate DATETIME DEFAULT GETDATE()
);

Use an ORM (e.g., Entity Framework) or direct SQL queries to insert data into the database.


Step 5: Use Event-Driven Updates

To ensure real-time synchronization:

Configure Azure AD B2C to call a webhook whenever a user registers or updates their information.

Process the webhook payload in your backend and save the updates in your database.


Step 6: Periodic Synchronization (Optional)

Set up a scheduled job to periodically fetch all user data from Azure B2C and sync it with your database.


